{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\njson.dump({\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Registers the one identified direction from this run's evidence that has no experiment yet, so it is preserved as a sourced question with a concrete discriminator rather than only as a sentence in a limitation. Nothing else changes.\\\",\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\n  \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@q_stale_snapshot_propagation\\\",\n  \\\"question\\\":\\\"Can the configuration state that a node writes into its snapshot metadata - which this run shows can be an older or empty membership even though the node's log establishes a newer one - reach another node through InstallSnapshot? A leader ships its newest snapshot to a follower whose next index lies below its compacted log start, and installSnapshot installs that snapshot's committed configuration and index (raft.go:1960-1961) before the follower applies the entries the leader sends above the snapshot index.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_snapshot_carries_config\\\",\\\"src_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"src_process_config_entry\\\",\\\"src_snapshot_cadence\\\",\\\"src_quorum_size\\\",\\\"src_commitment_from_config\\\"],\n  \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"Two outcomes are both plausible from the source. If the stale configuration recorded in a leader's snapshot is corrected by the configuration entries the leader re-sends above the snapshot index, the propagation is transient and only the snapshot's own index and membership are wrong until those entries arrive; if the intervening configuration entries have been trimmed from the leader's log, or the leader's own tracked configuration is the stale one so that the entries it sends continue it, the receiving node's decision state stays on the older membership, which would extend the defect's reach to a node whose own log and stores were never damaged.\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Build a group whose leader has a compacted log and a snapshot carrying an older configuration (raise TrailingLogs appropriately, take the snapshot before a committed removal, then restart the leader with the replay enabled so its tracked configuration is the snapshot's), add a fresh voter with an empty log, and compare the joiner's tracked configuration after it installs the snapshot and after it applies the entries the leader sends above the snapshot index, against the configuration entry list in the leader's log and against the committed configuration. The transient hypothesis predicts the joiner's configuration converges to the committed one once those entries arrive; the persistent hypothesis predicts it stays at the snapshot's older membership and that the entries above the snapshot index do not contain the configuration entries needed to correct it.\\\"\n }]\n},open('update45.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update45.json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"\nimport sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint('valid',d['valid'],'no_change',d.get('no_change'))\nfor x in d.get('diagnostics',[])[:6]: print(x['paths'],x['message'])\nprint([(e['object'],e['action']) for e in d.get('effects',[])])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
